{
  "title": "Hypnotoad",
  "about": "ALL GLORY TO THE HYPNOTOAD. Drawn front-on and symmetrical, which is how he is usually seen and the most hypnotic way to put anything on a wall. He keeps his own colours whatever the show hue is doing -- olive and cream, yellow eyes, black splat of a pupil -- because a Hypnotoad in the wrong colours is not Hypnotoad; Tint overrules that if you want him recoloured. Everything behind him takes the hue instead: wavy concentric hypno rings on a small quantised palette, with sacred geometry drawn over them (Flower of Life, Metatron's Cube, or a ring-and-spoke mandala). Drawn as flat vector -- no outline, the form coming from where one colour stops and the next starts, with a shading brown for the brow and the haunches. The flat artwork has no outline because it sits on a flat card; these rings are not one, so he gets a thin dark keyline by default to hold him off the background -- Keyline 0 takes it away again, and the collar is off by default because he reads better without it. The eyes do the work: a brown socket, flat concentric bands of yellow and orange run outward from the middle at their own speed in cycles per beat. Reactivity is the standard three slots, see docs/reactive.md.",
